\paperw12240\paperh15840\margl1800\margr1800\margt1440\margb1440\f0\fs24\cf0
\pard\plain \fi720\sl288\slmult1\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri shuffled onto Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s white wood, elevated veranda. The space was enclosed by a diamond trellis, thick with vines. No slipshod carpentry here; the stout boards under his feet were firm in their seats, and the clean joinery of the trellis professed a mastery of craft. The fiddleback pattern in the trellis wood shimmered, thanks to the burgeon he\u8217\'92d swallowed. If he was lucky, and the burgeon was strong, then in about a finger\u8217\'92s time, textures would start to bleed. In half a hand, he would not be able to separate the edges of the wood, the thorny vine, and the blue splotches of sky behind them. They would swirl together, pulse and breathe\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 one solid, flexing sheet.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 This veranda was the perfect place get high. If only it weren\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t smack in the middle of Vigram\u8217\'92s leech farm. He peeked through the diamond gaps in the trellis and was greeted with the horror that was twelve, massive, man-made leech lakes. Dark, rippling waters. Leeches swarmed in such numbers that they looked like black undulating clouds of mud.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The edges of the nearest lakes were lined with roofless stalls, with each stall penning a live animal into the shallows. Goats, horses, cows; any animal larger than a large dog would do. They were each slumped onto support beams. Their snouts were tied into bags of intoxicating freeweed smoke. This was not an act of beneficence to inure them to the pain, it was Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s way of keeping his peaceful country air free of their wild moaning.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The rest of the estate was mostly flies and marshgrass. The sky was cloudy with the kind of tall, mountainous clouds that swallowed landscape paintings whole, the kind that cast broad shadows down upon the world to pull the viewer through the distance, as they pulled Mandri now, all the way out to the sparkling blue line on the horizon which was the sea.}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1  And that sparkle was especially bright, rivaling the sun. The high from these down-valley burgeons could make textures slide and edges bleed, but the chief effect was that anything bright would sparkle\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 the sunlit cloudrims, the seashine, every tight specular reflection would sparkle like a twinkling star.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf1 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I made this myself,\u8221\'94 Vigram said as he unfolded a tall easel. Mandri doubted it.}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Brewed the glue, hammered the fittings. I should say that I\u8217\'92m proud of it.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Are you sure you want to do this here?\u8221\'94 Mandri asked as he leaned against the trellis.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Why not here?\u8221\'94 said Vigram.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri eyed the distressed animals in the lakes below. They were shaved down to the pink skin like criminals, poor things. Reduced to bags of blood. Leechmen waded between the stalls to trowel off the largest leeches and toss them into grass baskets. Those leeches which weren\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t engaged in the constant struggle for the cleanest spot of flesh were busy mating. It was a bit of an orgy down there.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Well,\u8221\'94 Mandri said as he fumbled about for a convenient excuse to get away from the sight and smell of death. He couldn\u8217\'92t think straight because of the burgeon. There was also the fact that he\u8217\'92d eaten more than his fill of Meskalimi leech, so all those goats, horses, and cows were suffering in leech paradise on account of him. What right did he have to look away?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Disgusted with himself, he turned his eyes to the vines overhead and saw the sun peeking through them. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93These vines aren\u8217\'92t yet thick enough for a solid shadow,\u8221\'94 he said. \u8220\'93A dappled light will fall upon the sitter, and that will make things difficult.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He held his hand out and turned it through the spotted light to demonstrate the effect.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93My dear Mandriiii,\u8221\'94 Vigram said with a provincial drawl that he\u8217\'92d done well to mask, until now. \u8220\'93The patterns of light and shadow are a magical vesture.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Well, we can worry about magical vestures when we\u8217\'92ve mastered the basics.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93No,\u8221\'94 Vigram said firmly, long beard wiggling. \u8220\'93I won\u8217\'92t have it any other way. A magical vesture for a magical subject.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 As if bidden from the heavens by Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s words, two young men hauled a marble bust of Vigram\u8217\'92s head out onto the veranda. Mandri wouldn\u8217\'92t have recognized the bust as Vigram if Vigram\u8217\'92s name weren\u8217\'92t engraved into the chunky base. It was an idealized version of the man, with less fat in the cheeks and a clearer jaw. And it had hair\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0  a flat curly mat of hair sort of haloed the skull. The beard was much shorter, and trimmed. The brow had an imperious aspect, a warrior\u8217\'92s glare. Essentially, it was regal. The only thing it was missing was a Lordly crown.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re going to paint a self-portrait?\u8221\'94 Mandri asked.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What? No,\u8221\'94 Vigram said, perplexed. \u8220\'93Mandri, }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 you}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  are the painter. I\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92m here to watch you give a demonstration. I know you didn\u8217\'92t bring any materials, but I\u8217\'92ve plenty here.\u8221\'94 He knuckle-knocked the top of a square taboret he\u8217\'92d set up next to the easel. He pulled one of the drawers out to show Mandri the packed rows of little clay jars. \u8220\'93Paints, brushes, turpentine, linseed, and I\u8217\'92ve a safflower and clove dip here, my own concoction, it will keep the brushes wet in the event we move into an extended session. Everything\u8217\'92s here. Nothing but the best.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I see\u8230\'85\u8221\'94 Mandri muttered.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He crossed his arms and pinched his lip.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 How was he going to get out of this?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He couldn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t paint, not in his current state. The burgeonsight was coming on strong; Vigram\u8217\'92s long brown beard looked like a flowing mudslide. There was every chance, that in half a finger, he might not be able to recognize his own hand if it were standing right in front of his face, because these down-valley burgeons could duplicate things. It only happened sometimes, but when it did, he could not find his hand amidst a splay of twenty or so hands, all with their pinkies and thumbs melting into each other.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He had eaten the burgeon on the assumption that Vigram would be the one painting, and that he would be staring over Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s shoulder. He could bullshit his way through a lesson by spouting off a few general tips and structural advice that would be applicable to any beginner\u8217\'92s work. But to actually paint? Not likely. The white wood planks under his feet were starting to bend. How was he supposed to draw a straight line, or keep things in proportion?}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I need to know where you\u8217\'92re at,\u8221\'94 he finally said. \u8220\'93So, for this first lesson, I would prefer to watch you paint. I mean, I haven\u8217\'92t even seen anything you\u8217\'92ve done. If I\u8217\'92m going to tailor my instruction, I need to know your skill level.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93No,\u8221\'94 Vigram said bluntly. \u8220\'93We will do this my way. I want to watch you work. It will give me insight into your methods.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Vigram,\u8221\'94 Mandri said as he rubbed his temples, \u8220\'93if I\u8217\'92m going to instruct you, then  you need to let me instruct you.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I should mention that I learn better by watching.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Nobody learns better by watching,\u8221\'94 Mandri moaned. \u8220\'93You learn by }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 doing}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 .\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll learn fine enough by watching.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You don\u8217\'92t get it,\u8221\'94 Mandri said . \u8220\'93Look, I\u8217\'92m going to be blunt with you, so take this how you will\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 the fact that you even want someone to teach you is not a positive sign. This happens a lot\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 people want to skip all the effort of figuring things out for themselves and so they jump straight to copying the way a master works. I mean, I\u8217\'92m not saying I\u8217\'92m a master, the point is, that\u8217\'92s not\u8230\'85it\u8217\'92s counterproductive.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You mean to tell me, that you\u8217\'92ve never watched another painter give a demonstration?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Sure, but look, you don\u8217\'92t want to know how }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 I}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  paint a face. You need to figure out how }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 you}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  paint a face. If you just copy the way that I work, you\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92re not really learning. You\u8217\'92re not growing into yourself as an artist. In five years, you\u8217\'92ll look at your own work and realize that you haven\u8217\'92t done a damned thing but waste your time.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mandri, Mandri, Mandri,\u8221\'94 Vigram clucked. \u8220\'93Have you not heard a single thing I\u8217\'92ve said this whole time? White light, boy! Next you\u8217\'92ll speak of }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 styles}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0 ! Let\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s have no more of this degeneracy. A man will commune with forces greater than himself, or he will not. Now. You will stand here,\u8221\'94 he stood himself before the easel and lifted a large canvas up onto it. \u8220\'93And I will watch you paint. You will articulate your decisions as you make them. I will ask clarifying questions as they come. If you don\u8217\'92t want to do that, then you will leave. Will you stay, or will you leave?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Oh, I\u8217\'92ll stay,\u8221\'94 Mandri said, and he gave a little laugh as though he were being the better man. \u8220\'93But you need to understand that you\u8217\'92re not going to get better unless you paint, and paint often.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I know it,\u8221\'94 Vigram said, \u8220\'93Better than you, I should say. But for now, }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 you}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  will paint.\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94 Then he drew back and shouted over his shoulder, \u8220\'93Someone quiet that animal!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 An old, yellow headed ox was mooing down in the nearest leech lake. It was angry at being stuck inside its stall, and also, at being bled to death. It mooed again. It bucked against its restraints, then gave a desperate, plaintive plea: \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mrruuuuuu!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Get that beast\u8217\'92s snout stuck in some weed!\u8221\'94 Vigram roared. Down below, a few leechmen stumbled out of their marshgrass daydreams. They adjusted their wide-brim hats, and scurried towards the ox. They splashed belly-deep through the water. The burgeon had all that splashing sparkling like a spill of diamonds.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri sighed a sigh for the old ox. He wished he had the courage to moo like that. He privately resolved to never eat a Meskalimi leech again. Then he did what he was told to do. He pulled the paints and solvents out of the taboret, set up a pallette from He started at that sheet of white as though it were an old enemy. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He rummaged through the  he picked up stick of soft charcoal, the lesson began.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 An old, yellow headed ox was mooing down in the nearest leech lake. It was angry at being stuck inside its stall, and also, at being bled to death. It mooed again. It bucked against its restraints, then gave a desperate, plaintive plea: \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mrruuuuuu!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Get that beast\u8217\'92s snout stuck in some weed!\u8221\'94 Vigram roared. Down below, a few leechmen stumbled out of their marshgrass daydreams. They adjusted their wide-brim hats, and scurried towards the ox. \u8220\'93And you,\u8221\'94 Vigram said to Mandri, \u8220\'93help Pel onto her stool. I\u8217\'92ll ready the canvas and paint.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri sighed a sigh for the old ox. He wished he had the courage to moo like that. He privately resolved to never eat a Meskalimi leech again. Then he did what he was told and moved to help Pel up onto her high-legged stool, though this was unnecessary, because Pel was tall enough that she could simply sit down. He helped her anyways, and her fingers lingered on his wrist. He began to suspect that she had some experience as a torturer.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram eventually settled down and positioned himself in front of the canvas. When he picked up stick of soft charcoal, the lesson began.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The first exploratory marks were always difficult. Every work of art must be built on a firm foundation; get it wrong and everything that comes after will be wrong as well. Unfortunately for Vigram, he had that all too common beginner\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s habit of refusing to use his god damned brain. He started drawing wherever his hand happened to land, and whatever happened next was up to Solraheen. The end result was that Pel\u8217\'92s head was half the size it needed to be. It was also too left-of-center. There\u8217\'92d be an awkward expanse behind her healthy sweep of hair.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Hold on,\u8221\'94 Vigram said. \u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re moving too fast.\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri looked at the oval he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d drawn. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You need to tell me what you\u8217\'92re thinking,\u8221\'94 Vigram said. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Well, I\u8217\'92m not thinking of this as a portrait\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 not yet. All we have right now is an oval, a rectangular canvas, and where that oval sits on that canvas. All I\u8217\'92m doing is putting an oval on a rectangle.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Right.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93So I\u8217\'92m thinking, where\u8217\'92s the best place to put that oval? How big should it be? I have the whole canvas here, and maybe I haven\u8217\'92t quite used it.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You\u8217\'92ve told me all this before.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram rubbed the marks away with his palm.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He stepped back.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He studied Pel.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He stepped again to the canvas, then scratched another black oval exactly where the first had been.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Is that better?\u8221\'94 Vigram asked with all the awareness of a potted plant. \u8220\'93You think it needs to be bigger?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Why not,\u8221\'94 Mandri said, and he drew the oval again, but only slightly larger. From then on, every other mark he made was accompanied by a look back to Mandri for reassurance. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93How do you know,\u8221\'94 Vigram said, \u8220\'93when the mark you\u8217\'92ve made is correct?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93They\u8217\'92re never correct.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 There was a glimmer of understanding in Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s eye, but just as soon as it came it faded. \u8220\'93If the mark is always wrong, then how can you ever move past it? You\u8217\'92ll be redrawing the same line over and over again.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You move on when you can\u8217\'92t stand to try anymore.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93That sounds miserable.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It is,\u8221\'94 Mandri said, feeling understood. \u8220\'93You should be defeated by the time you\u8217\'92ve finished. I\u8217\'92ve always thought that you should never feel good about what you\u8217\'92re doing, because that means you\u8217\'92re not trying hard enough. Now, I\u8217\'92ll finish\u8230\'85I\u8217\'92ll finish the basic shapes.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Alright.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8216\'91finished\u8217\'92 the \u8216\'91basic shapes\u8217\'92. He looked to Mandri for final approval.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mandri, I don\u8217\'92t have you here to watch you draw. I\u8217\'92m here to watch you paint.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0  \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93But you need to understand the importance of the drawing. You\u8217\'92re always drawing. Even when painting, you are drawing.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I know,\u8221\'94 Vigram grumbled. \u8220\'93You talk about it all the time.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram made to redraw the too-large chin, but was interrupted by a loud, mournful ox bellow.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Damn it!\u8221\'94 Vigram cried, shaking his fist.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Focus,\u8221\'94 Mandri said. \u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t get distracted. Let your men do their job.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93If they were doing their job, I wouldn\u8217\'92t have heard that noise!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Please,\u8221\'94 Mandri repeated. \u8220\'93Focus.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram closed his eyes and took a deep breath. When he next looked upon his canvas, he was resolved: \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m done drawing! I\u8217\'92m here to paint!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He tossed his charcoal over his shoulder and picked up his favorite brush. He mixed a bluish shade of bronze\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 the color of the jaw of a Jandri man who keeps a close shave\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 and then he threw down the first splotches of color in a flurry. He wasn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t painting so much as he was assaulting the canvas. And Sol\u8217\'92s light, that bentberry fiber weave was innocent. Expensive, too, coveted for its depth of feeling, for how it made the undertones blush. Troubled by Vigram\u8217\'92s hand, those tones were bruised and near to bleeding. It was a very confused slapping around.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri had to look away.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 He glanced in Pel\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s direction.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The moment his eyes wandered down the depth of her neckline, the corner of her lip perked up. He kept looking, because why else would she wear that cut if not to catch him staring? Why else would she be swimming in that perfume? Why bite that honeyed, aching lip? Why, if Solraheen\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s last will and testament was not inciting him to stare, why did the soft shadows of the vines overhead frame her piercing eyes with the most magnificent golden light? A magical vesture indeed. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Mandri, stop flirting with my muse.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I am not flirting,\u8221\'94 Mandri claimed. \u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m checking proportions.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Yes, and how are her proportions?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The old goat\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s eyebrows jumped suggestively. Pel huffed in annoyance. The yellow headed ox weighed in with an oxen roar.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93MRRRRRUUUUUUUUUUUUU!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93That\u8217\'92s it!\u8221\'94 Vigram shouted.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Below, in the leech lake, two leechmen tried to force the yellow-headed ox\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s snout into a bag of freeweed smoke. But the men were too skinny. The ox bucked them both into the air, then broke its constraints and jumped its rail. The beast tore through the leech lake, kicking up waves of confused, copulating leeches. Seeing this, Mandri\u8217\'92s spirit soared, and he clenched his fist in a quiet cheer.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Stop that ox!\u8221\'94 Vigram shouted as he pointed with his loaded brush. \u8220\'93There\u8217\'92s a five silver-strings of leeches attached to that beast! If you don\u8217\'92t\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 \u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Vigram,\u8221\'94 Mandri said firmly. \u8220\'93You\u8217\'92ll make a bad habit if you keep stopping in the middle of the work.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t tell me what to do, boy! On }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 my}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  farm!?\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Focus! Let it go.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram drew up in rage. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t ask me to let go of my principles! That animal }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 defies}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  me.\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram rushed to a window in the trellis and ordered his men to greater action. A squad was gathered. They hunted as a pack. Vigram conducted their movements with his brush. They soon had the ox surrounded in the shallows of a distant lake. The ox, legs wide like a waterbug, fended off their sharpened sticks with its stubbed horns. Mooing, bleeding, fighting for its life, it charged the smallest leechman. The little man dove into the infested waters, and again, the ox was loose.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93DAMN IT ALL!\u8221\'94 Vigram screamed.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s chest swelled with both pity and admiration. Such feeling could not be tamed. He had to do something.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What if I bought it?\u8221\'94 he asked.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Vigram\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s rage was blunted by sheer confusion. He turned around.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Mandri found his confidence and said, \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92ll buy the ox off you.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Why?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93So that we can continue with the lesson. I\u8217\'92d like to get home before dark.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Nonsense. We\u8217\'92ll come to it.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93I\u8217\'92m serious. I\u8217\'92ll buy it.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93That decrepit thing? Are you looking to sacrifice it? The gods are all dead, you know this. Are you making fun of me?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What? No.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Do you }{\f1\fs24\b0\i1 judge}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0  me, boy?\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93This isn\u8217\'92t about you, Vigram. I respect the creature. It\u8217\'92s got fight.\u8221\'94}}